 # Business Rules — PegaFila
 
-Domain document for **PegaFilaWeb** — repository **frontend, backend and totem API** (Laravel monolith). Derived from product requirements. Core domain issuance is implemented via `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (ticket into an active queue) and deterministic call-next via `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (three call modes + 3-ticket fairness); HTTP, Livewire, and billing remain future work.
+Domain document for **PegaFilaWeb** — repository **frontend, backend and totem API** (Laravel monolith). Derived from product requirements. Core domain issuance is implemented via `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (ticket into an active queue) and deterministic call-next via `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (three call modes + 3-ticket fairness). Queue lifecycle (`CreateQueue`, `UpdateQueue`) and per-queue employee grants (`SetQueueAccess`) are implemented as domain actions, with `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` as the single authorization source of truth. HTTP, Livewire screens, and billing remain future work.
 
 ## MVP Scope
 
@@ -98,7 +98,16 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths reject inactive queues and enforce `QueuePolicy::call`; HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+
+### Queue lifecycle and access
+
+- **Creation:** owner/admin of the entity only. `CreateQueue` trims the name (1–255 chars), derives `slug = Str::slug(name)` unless an explicit slug is given (also slugified), and creates an **active** queue.
+- **Slug uniqueness:** a slug is unique **within an entity**; the same slug may exist in another entity. Duplicates (including a lost DB race) surface as `ValidationException`, never a raw query error.
+- **Update:** owner/admin of the queue's entity only. `UpdateQueue` accepts any combination of name, slug, and `is_active` (null leaves the value unchanged). Keeping the queue's own slug is allowed.
+- **No hard delete:** a queue is retired by setting `is_active = false`. Its tickets are preserved; issuing or calling on it keeps failing with `InactiveQueueException`. There is no delete/remove/destroy queue action.
+- **Employee grants:** `queue_access` links an `entity_membership` to a queue with a JSON list of permissions. Today the only permission is `call` (`App\Enums\QueuePermission::Call`). A manager sets grants through `SetQueueAccess`: a non-empty list upserts, an empty list revokes. Unknown/non-string permissions and membership/queue entity mismatches are `ValidationException`; non-managers are denied with `AuthorizationException`.
+- **Call authorization:** managers (owner/admin) may always call on their entity's queues. An employee may call only on a queue with a `queue_access` row whose `permissions` array contains `call`. Everyone else is denied, and a corrupted non-list permissions value denies. Grants and revocations write `queue.access.granted` / `queue.access.revoked` to the `audit` log channel with `actor_id`, `queue_id`, and `entity_membership_id`.
 
 ### Priority
 
